# ── B3 BEHAVIOURALLY: a set-empty half is still a DECLARED server — RETIRED (slice Z3) ───────────────
# The wrapper's frozen preamble carried the typed server pair across a process
# boundary, and the set-not-nonempty rule existed because `${VAR:-}` dropped a
# set-empty half on the way. There is no boundary left to drop it at: AE_TMUX_SERVER
# and AE_TMUX_SERVER_KIND are read once, by the core, as an env DOOR. The rule moved
